"Net control" (haha, more like "net out-of-control") for the Palo Alto Amateur Radio Club CW simplified practice net-after-the-net.   This is for our CW beginners to start getting on the air.      People are just getting on the air so there are plenty of mistakes, detours off-script, etc. just like in real qso's.   Also I am just getting the hang of being a CW net controller.    Taking it all in stride is one of the skills we're building.    Non-club members are welcome to join and it's good practice for our learners (including me trying to run it while learning myself) -- please don't be offended if we keep it short; we're just trying not to overwhelm folks many of whom are really sweating (including me!)

A good general resource for beginners is at https://skccgroup.com/member_services/beginners_corner/#Typical-QSO .  (applies to any type of key)

We coordinate in voice on the N6NFI 2m repeater (reachable via echolink) at around 9:00pm Mondays Pacific time, figure out a frequency, and go from there.    We're usually on 7.059 but will QSY to avoid interfering with anyone else.   We stick around on the repeater so there is a voice back-channel so people don't get completely lost.

SIMPLIFIED CW PRACTICE NET SCRIPT 


QRL?

------------------ introduction and call for checkins -----------------

GE PAARA PRACTICE NET DE W6EFI OP CONNIE NC =
CALLSIGNS NOW QNI? K

(callsign1)

(callsign1) TU UR 5nn PSE AS = QNI? K

(callsign2) 

TU (callsign2) UR 5nn PSE AS = QNI? K

(callsign3) IO     (IO indicates "in and out" - skip me during the comment round.  See below)

TU (callsign3) UR 5nn 73 = QNI? K    (say 73 now to any IO checker-inner)

etc

-------------------- comment round -- call people one at a time, ask question -----------

OK LET'S START DE W6EFI NC =

(callsign1) GE PSE SEND UR NAME ES NAME TWO COLORS BK    (or some other simple question)

name is ben colors are blue es fuchsia de (callsign1) k

TU ben 73 DE W6EFI NEXT =

(callsign2) GE PSE SEND UR NAME ES NAME TWO COLORS BK    (or some other question)

name is alice colors are sepia es cerulean de (callsign2) k 

TU alice 73 DE W6EFI NEXT = 

etc

---------------- end of list, see if there are any late checkins ----------

THIS IS THE PAARA PRACTICE NET NC W6EFI =

QNI?

(see if there are any other takers)

NIL =     (nothing heard)

TU ALL GN ES 73 QNF SK DE W6EFI    (QNF = freq returned to normal use)

-----------------------------------------------
-----------------------------------------------

If you just want to drop in your callsign and not participate
in the comment round: just append IO or QNX or QNO to your callsign 

W6EFI IO
(or)
W6EFI QNX
(or)
W6EFI QNO

OR you can just not respond when called during the comment round -- that is okay!
